\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Simulations, 500 Monte Carlo repetitions and $B=999$. (a--b) Joint coverage and mean width of simultaneous intervals versus the latent-Gaussian ICC parameter; error bars are $\pm 1.96$ Monte Carlo standard errors (coverage bars clipped to $[0,1]$). ``Raw paired'' applies bootstrap-$t$ directly to root resamples; ``cluster marginal'' has no multiplicity correction; ``separate risk'' derives contrasts from simultaneous absolute-risk intervals and discards paired covariance. (c) Reference-population robust regret at $\rho =1$ as one represented environment increasingly reverses its spurious signal; bands are $\pm 1.96$ Monte Carlo standard errors. (d) HRMS confidence-set size and robust-oracle coverage.}}{6}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:simulation}{{2}{6}{Simulations, 500 Monte Carlo repetitions and $B=999$. (a--b) Joint coverage and mean width of simultaneous intervals versus the latent-Gaussian ICC parameter; error bars are $\pm 1.96$ Monte Carlo standard errors (coverage bars clipped to $[0,1]$). ``Raw paired'' applies bootstrap-$t$ directly to root resamples; ``cluster marginal'' has no multiplicity correction; ``separate risk'' derives contrasts from simultaneous absolute-risk intervals and discards paired covariance. (c) Reference-population robust regret at $\rho =1$ as one represented environment increasingly reverses its spurious signal; bands are $\pm 1.96$ Monte Carlo standard errors. (d) HRMS confidence-set size and robust-oracle coverage}{figure.2}{}}
